>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `clear_rules`

``` hol4
simpLib.clear_rules : simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes the rules from a simpset, keeping its settings.

`clear_rules ss` removes the rewrites, conversions, congruences, decision
procedures, loopers and fragments of `ss`. It keeps the rewrite maker, the
limit, the solvers, the subgoaler, the side-condition depth and the term
order. Simplifying with `clear_rules ss` and theorems `ths` therefore uses
`ths` alone, under the settings of `ss`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpLib.SIMP_CONV (simpLib.clear_rules ss)
     [boolTheory.AND_CLAUSES] “p ∧ T ∧ (x:num = x)”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpLib.set_cond_depth),
[`simpLib.set_subgoaler`](#simpLib.set_subgoaler).
